+# The Daily Grind
+
+Static HTML site. No build step is required.
+
+## INP diagnostics
+
+`assets/inp-diagnostics.mjs` uses the locally vendored Google `web-vitals`
+attribution library (version 6.2.3, Apache-2.0) to measure Interaction to Next
+Paint. The original distribution and license are in `assets/vendor/`.
+Library source: https://github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/tree/v6.2.3
+
+INP candidates above 200 ms produce a console warning. Each report contains
+the interaction target and type, input delay, handler processing duration,
+presentation delay, and the longest overlapping script when available.
+The dominant timing phase suggests where to investigate; it does not prove
+causality. Script and layout attribution depends on browser support for the
+Long Animation Frames API; missing data is left undefined or null.
+
+The latest report is available as `window.inpDiagnostics`. To connect an
+existing analytics system, listen for reports:
+
+```js
+window.addEventListener('inp-diagnostic', ({ detail }) => {
+  // Forward detail to your existing telemetry integration here.
+});
+```
+
+No reports are sent over the network by this code. Reports use the same metric
+`id` as candidates change; an analytics integration should update by ID rather
+than count every callback as a separate page visit. Values during the visit
+are provisional, and the library also reports changes when the page is hidden.
+Reports require supported Event Timing APIs and a qualifying interaction;
+an absent report does not establish good INP. No key values or element text
+are captured, but selectors and script URLs should be reviewed before sending
+reports to analytics.
